{#
    The document, and nothing around it. No bar, no rail, no footer. What the
    page puts around the article is the site's navigation. A reader who
    followed a link here has that in the links inside it.

    What the page carries in its head, the twin carries as front matter. The
    title, what the page is about, the page this is the twin of, and every
    field the author wrote above the title. It is the first byte of the file,
    because that is the only place a reader reads front matter as such.
#}
{%- autoescape false -%}
{%- set opening = node|md_opening -%}
{%- set head -%}
title: {{ node.pageTitle|md_yaml }}
{% if opening %}description: {{ opening|md_yaml }}
{% endif %}canonical: {{ env.currentFileName|split('/')|last }}.html
{% for headerNode in node.headerNodes %}{{ renderNode(headerNode) }}
{% endfor %}
{%- endset -%}
---
{{ head|split("\n")|map(line => line|trim)|filter(line => line)|join("\n") }}
---

{% set body -%}
{% for child in node.children %}{{ renderNode(child)|md_tidy }}

{% endfor %}
{%- endset -%}
{{ body|md_tidy }}
{% endautoescape %}
